WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.270
This is Bao Bao.

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:06.240
She was born in 2013 at the National Zoo in
Washington, DC.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.400
Here she is biting her foot.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.879
Here she is in the snow.

00:00:09.879 --> 00:00:16.160
And here she is in a jumbo-sized FedEx crate
bound for a one-way trip to Chengdu, China.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.790
Bao Bao left because she was never ours to
keep.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:23.620
Her parents, Mei Xiang and Tian Tian, came from
China 17 years ago.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:27.150
But they weren’t a gift – they were a loan.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.560
And that loan stipulated their offspring will
also belong to China,

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.730
as do almost all of the pandas in zoos worldwide.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:39.790
Pandas’ natural habitat exists entirely
within the borders of one country.

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:45.210
And that means these animals are more than
just mascots for China: they’re also tools

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:51.700
in China’s global diplomatic strategy.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:57.110
What China figured out as it kind of became
more of an international power in the second

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:00.890
half of the 20th century was that this was
something it could use to its advantage.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:05.280
Pandas have been part of Chinese foreign policy
since at least the 1950s.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.890
Initially, it was just kind of given in the
same way that you know governments have usually

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:12.610
given exotic animals to others.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:14.460
It gave pandas to its allies.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:19.920
Then after pandas officially became endangered,
and that looked kind of tacky, they started

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:27.590
giving pandas as loans. In return, the receiving
zoos pay $1 million, per panda, each year

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:28.940
in fees.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:34.480
And if a cub is born, zoos pay an extra “cub
tax” of $400,000.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:38.390
The thing is ... China doesn't give pandas to
any country that can put up the money for

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:40.720
a loan; it's much more selective than that.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:45.640
Researchers at the University of Oxford have
noticed a correlation between panda loans

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.490
and China’s international trade deals.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:53.860
In 2010, China realized that it needed to
find more market capacity to buy salmon.Their

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:58.360
traditional trade partner, who was Norway,
had been kind of... The Nobel Peace Prize

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:02.610
had gone to a Chinese dissident, China didn't
feel like rewarding that behavior,

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.409
so instead they turned to Scotland,

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:05.770
which also produced salmon,

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:10.380
also produced Land Rovers, which was something
else that the Chinese affluent class were

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:16.820
interested in, and so they inked that trade
deal and a panda was sent to the Edinburgh Zoo.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:20.560
But what China gives, it can also take away.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.870
Consider the case of Tai Shan, Bao Bao’s
older brother from DC.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:29.120
China had made it known toward the end of
2009 that it wanted to take back the panda

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.230
Tai Shan.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.370
It hadn't really set a date yet.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:37.610
Officials at the National zoo asked China
to extend his stay, but the answer was no.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:41.610
Experts suspect a couple of factors were involved
in that choice.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:46.989
One, President Obama met with the Dalai Lama,
who is a strong critic of the Chinese government

00:02:46.989 --> 00:02:51.480
and a fierce advocate for the independence
of Tibet, which the Chinese government denies.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:56.250
And second, the US announced an rms sale
to Taiwan, over Chinese objections.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:01.209
A week later, Tai Shan and another panda
from the Atlanta Zoo were on their way to

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:02.209
China.

00:03:02.209 --> 00:03:08.540
It considers pandas as kind of another arm
of diplomacy in the same way that, in the

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:13.790
event of a diplomatic spat, one country might
recall its ambassador or might impose economic

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:20.160
sanctions, China sees, or certainly appears
to see, from the way that its agreements go,

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:26.530
pandas as kind of a way to reinforce international
relationships that it's building and it wants

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:27.709
to continue.

00:03:27.709 --> 00:03:32.510
More recently, we saw China delay a panda
delivery following the disappearance of a

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:35.840
Malaysia Airlines plane carrying 152 Chinese
nationals.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:40.500
In 2014, Malaysia was all ready to get its
first panda.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:44.000
They had the enclosure ready at the zoo and all of that.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:49.180
And the day of the panda's supposed arrival
came and went because the Chinese government

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:54.269
was extremely frustrated with the Malaysian
government's investigation of the flight,

00:03:54.269 --> 00:03:59.880
didn't feel that it was doing enough, and so
kept the pandas for another month or two as

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:05.709
a way to demonstrate to the Malaysian government
that yeah, we've signed a regional trade deal

00:04:05.709 --> 00:04:09.610
with you, we're interested in pursuing a relationship,
but you're not making us super happy right

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:10.610
now.

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:15.870
Currently, the US still has 12 pandas, including
Bao Bao’s new little brother, Bei Bei.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:20.439
But future relations with China could change
that. It's entirely possible that, whether

00:04:20.439 --> 00:04:26.029
in a military respect in the South China Sea
or in a political respect with regards to Taiwan,

00:04:26.029 --> 00:04:30.909
that China will find good reason to feel that
the US is no longer interested in pursuing

00:04:30.909 --> 00:04:33.539
the kind of warm partnership that they've had.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:37.019
So what that means for panda diplomacy is
really anyone's guess.

